&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Developer Advocate at GitLab, you&#39;ll help technical audiences understand and use our intelligent orchestration platform where teams and their AI agents ship secure software faster. You&#39;ll go deep on the product, especially GitLab Duo Agent Platform and our newer capabilities, and continuously discover real-world workflows that teams care about. You&#39;ll turn that hands-on knowledge into demos, blog posts, videos, and presentations, and bring what you learn from customers and the developer community back to GitLab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses on showing the product in action and building relationships with customers and the community. You&#39;ll help cover events and work across U.S. and Canadian time zones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand GitLab&#39;s platform, especially our AI agent capabilities, and continuously find productive, real-world use cases worth showing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create product content, including videos, blog posts, presentations, and social clips that show key use cases for GitLab in the user interface and terminal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce video content end to end: script, record, and edit product walkthroughs and demos, and collaborate with GitLab&#39;s video team on longer or higher-production pieces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver product demos and participate in analyst briefings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with customers through webinars, customer meetings, and other conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the developer community by engaging on the GitLab forum and Discord, following the conversations happening on social platforms, in newsletters, and at events, and making sure GitLab has a voice in the ones that matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer technical questions that come through the sales team, and partner with support, sales, and product on developer-facing educational content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use hands-on product experience to share feedback with product teams and test new features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical research and analysis of the developer tools landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel requirement up to 20% for events and customer meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on technical experience. You understand how software gets built, with a focus on everything that happens after code is written, and can talk about it credibly with engineers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of artificial intelligence and its use in software development, from coding all the way to production. You have built and operated agentic systems and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to explain technical products clearly. You can demo a product, record a walkthrough, or speak at a conference without it feeling forced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in developer social platforms. You know what&#39;s interesting to the people we&#39;re trying to reach and can participate in the conversation with credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and self-direction. You&#39;re already finding the next thing worth talking about, following the right people, and noticing opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with customers, developers, or technical communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and collaborate across sales, engineering, product, and other teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Developer Advocacy team creates content that shows GitLab in use, engages with customers and the developer community, and brings hands-on product feedback to GitLab teams. The team also contributes technical research and analysis, while partnering with other groups to share its findings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$194,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Wholesale Director EMEA &amp;amp; APAC&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Wholesale&lt;/strong&gt; team based in &lt;strong&gt;Paris&lt;/strong&gt;, covering a maternity leave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fixed-term contract (CDD), starting &lt;strong&gt;early December 2026&lt;/strong&gt; for the duration of the absence of the employee being replaced — expected to run through approximately &lt;strong&gt;May 2027&lt;/strong&gt;, with the exact end date depending on the return of the employee on leave. A structured handover is planned in two steps: an initial transition with the outgoing Director around mid-December 2026, and a second handover at the end of the assignment, around her return in May 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key contributor within our &lt;strong&gt;Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt; team, the Wholesale Director EMEA &amp;amp; APAC steps into an existing commercial organization and ensures continuity of leadership for our EMEA &amp;amp; APAC wholesale business during the interim period. The role directly manages a team of four — &lt;strong&gt;two Wholesale Managers EU + ME/APAC&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;one ADV Manager EU&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;one Wholesale Support Intern&lt;/strong&gt; — and owns the commercial and operational performance of a multi-market portfolio operated through key accounts, agents, and franchise partners. The role also works closely with our &lt;strong&gt;Wholesale Strategic Advisor&lt;/strong&gt;, an internal resource who supports continuity throughout the assignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid position based at our Paris HQ, with a preference for in-person work. The role reports to the &lt;strong&gt;CEO&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day leadership to the two Wholesale Managers EU + ME/APAC, the ADV Manager EU, and the Wholesale Support Intern, ensuring business continuity and uninterrupted decision-making during the interim period&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the commercial performance of the ME &amp;amp; APAC wholesale portfolio — sell-in, sell-through, forecasting, and seasonal budgets across key accounts, agents, distributors, and franchise partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sell-in for any Paris showroom season(s) falling within the contract period: oversee collection presentation, negotiation, seasonal budgets, and payment terms with senior buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the network of agents, distributors, and franchise / shop-in-shop partners across ME and APAC: targets, seasonal action plans, brand standards, and performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure ADV operational execution through the ADV Manager: order management, Key Account shipping compliance, 3PL coordination, and delivery / stocklist reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary escalation point for key accounts and priority partners in EMEA &amp;amp; APAC for the duration of the assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Wholesale Strategic Advisor to ensure continuity on ongoing initiatives and institutional knowledge throughout the assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report portfolio performance directly to the CEO — sell-in/sell-out KPIs, budget vs. actuals, stock and delivery status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functionally with Merchandising, Production, Operations, and Finance to secure deliveries and resolve escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain continuity on any in-flight strategic initiatives (including agent-to-direct market transitions) without introducing new strategic shifts absent CEO sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete a structured handover with the outgoing Director in mid-December 2026, and prepare a full handover back to her ahead of her return around May 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in fashion wholesale, including proven experience managing a commercial team across an international, multi-market portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record as Wholesale Director, Area Manager, or senior Wholesale Manager, with solid knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;EMEA markets&lt;/strong&gt;; working familiarity with APAC market dynamics is expected, as the region is operated through agents and distributors rather than direct management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing agents, distributors, franchise / master-franchise partners, and key accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of sell-in / sell-out analysis, OTB logic, forecasting, and in-season performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing a Sales Administration / Order Management function (ERP, 3PL coordination, key account portal compliance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with B2B and ERP tools (JOOR, NuOrder, Cegid Orli, NetSuite or equivalent) and advanced Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English and French required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A confident, autonomous people manager, comfortable stepping into an existing team and reporting directly to executive leadership with minimal ramp-up time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available for a fixed-term assignment in Paris starting early December 2026, for the duration of the maternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At ANINE BING Paris, we combine creative ambition with a people-first culture. Expect generous time off (including RTT), flexible work, exclusive discounts on our collections, and private sales access — so you can live the brand as much as you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Style Perks: Enjoy a generous employee discount and seasonal wardrobe allotments — so you can live the brand, not just represent it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Base salary: commensurate with profile and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING seeks to empower its employees by providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and teammates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, Veteran status, or other legally protected characteristics. Diversity and inclusion is critical to our success as a global brand, and we seek to recruit, develop, and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More about ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is a Los Angeles-based fashion house founded in 2012 that blends elements of Scandinavian simplicity with American energy to offer modern wardrobe essentials for women seeking a timeless yet rebellious approach to everyday style. Since its launch, ANINE BING has evolved into a global brand, available in over 90 countries with a growing network of brick-and-mortar retail stores in key cities worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Powered by a global team of over 250 employees, ANINE BING is headquartered in Los Angeles and Paris, with additional offices in New York and Shanghai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Our Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Located just off the Champs-Élysées, our Paris headquarters at 1 Rue François 1er is a cornerstone of our international growth. As the home of our Product teams and other key functions, this space reflects our commitment to creativity, collaboration, and global perspective. As we continue to grow across Europe, our Paris office plays a central role in shaping the future of our brand.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is looking for an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;RTW Intern Designer (F/M)&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;PAP Studio&lt;/strong&gt; team based in &lt;strong&gt;Paris&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is an opportunity to help shape the next chapter of ANINE BING. As a key contributor within our &lt;strong&gt;Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt; team, the &lt;strong&gt;RTW Intern Designer&lt;/strong&gt; supports the PAP Studio in day-to-day coordination and collection development, bringing precision and creative energy to their work — supporting our global growth while staying grounded in the brand&#39;s DNA: refined, fast-moving, and always evolving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who thrives in a creative yet performance-driven environment. The ideal candidate combines a sharp eye for detail with a clear sense of the big picture, is comfortable moving between technical execution and creative research, and is energized by building something special—together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an internship based at our &lt;strong&gt;Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt;, in-person, for a &lt;strong&gt;minimum duration of 6 months&lt;/strong&gt;. The role reports to the &lt;strong&gt;Head of Design&lt;/strong&gt;, with a dotted line to the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Designer&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Studio coordination &amp;amp; collection support:&lt;/strong&gt; produce technical drawings on Illustrator, update and maintain technical files (tech packs), and keep collection boards, moodboards, and working boards current throughout the season.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design execution:&lt;/strong&gt; color and finish sketches, build collection boards, produce presentation mock-ups and supports, and develop digital color ranges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research:&lt;/strong&gt; conduct iconographic research on styles, finishes, materials and details, and develop visual references to support collection direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;File management:&lt;/strong&gt; organize and maintain collection files and digital archives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fittings &amp;amp; prototype follow-up:&lt;/strong&gt; assist at proto fittings, style-outs and shopping sessions; take photos and update technical drawings and annotations following each fitting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prototype tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; archive and organize fitting photos and information, and track modifications made to styles throughout development; help prepare fittings (silhouettes, looks, accessories, visual supports).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General studio support:&lt;/strong&gt; prepare documents and boards for collection presentations and meetings, maintain creative and trend watch, and support the studio&#39;s day-to-day organization as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final-year student at a fashion design school, available for a &lt;strong&gt;minimum 6-month internship&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced proficiency in Photoshop and Illustrator is mandatory&lt;/strong&gt;, including technical drawing execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and rigor in following technical and creative briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English required; French professional proficiency is a plus given the Paris-based team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized, proactive, and comfortable working across parallel priorities in a creative, performance-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At ANINE BING Paris, we combine creative ambition with a people-first culture, exclusive discounts on our collections, and private sales access — so you can live the brand as much as you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
